{"chunk_id": "f48becfd1723", "text": "This section continues the description of sacred pilgrimage sites (tirthas) recounted to Yudhishthira, emphasizing regions associated with ancient sacrifices, sages, and rivers such as Saraswati and Drisadwati. The narrative highlights holy places like Gangadwara and the hermitage of Badrinath (Vadari), portrayed as the dwelling of Narayana, where gods and rishis gather and where the divine presence makes the entire universe\u2019s sanctity converge. The passage stresses that visiting these places with ascetics brings spiritual merit and relief from anxiety. The scene then shifts: the sage Lomasa arrives and reports news from heaven. He has seen Arjuna seated beside Indra, having gained powerful celestial weapons\u2014including the Brahma\u2011sira\u2014and mastery of arts. Indra\u2019s message urges Yudhishthira to practice austerities while awaiting Arjuna\u2019s return, foreshadowing future conflicts with mighty warriors like Karna.\nLomasa arrives with news from Indra: Arjuna in heaven has gained powerful celestial weapons and skills, while Yudhishthira is urged to continue ascetic practices.\nThemes: pilgrimage sites, divine weapons, asceticism, Arjuna in heaven, divine messages", "vector": [0.012495807372033596, -0.013585046865046024, 0.0019078601617366076, 0.009004829451441765, -0.0003896482812706381, 0.03526158630847931, -0.04043039679527283, -0.019592776894569397, -0.007577316835522652, -0.016277700662612915, 0.010878861881792545, 0.0009995969012379646, 0.0032930884044617414, -0.004285919945687056, -0.0036499665584415197, -0.001417364226654172, 0.04224354028701782, -0.008781569078564644, 0.01780669391155243, -0.004844070412218571, -0.012949093244969845, -0.001813143608160317, -0.0007657656678929925, 0.01257022749632597, -0.014667520299553871, 0.02717009373009205, 0.020147543400526047, -0.021811848506331444, -0.007103734649717808, -0.0057134320959448814, -0.014315715990960598, -0.009228089824318886, -0.010824738070368767